e sum of the measures of the interior angles of any triangle is always equal to $180^\\circ$.*\n\nFor example, in $\\triangle ABC$ shown above, the interior angle theorem tells us that\n\n$$\nm\\angle{A} + m\\angle{B} + m\\angle{C} = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we know the measures of two angles in a triangle, we can calculate the value of the other." 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186080052 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186080053 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186080054 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186080055 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186080056 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487614 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487631 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487824 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186487941 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186080051 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488029 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186080051 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488029 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083179 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488258 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083179 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488281 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083180 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488182 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083180 1038 #edb/ref 17592186488278 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083526 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186083526 1071 "![](images/e0/e07a67e287b43cad2785d717393a3868803b94dffed14040fdf1329dd6bc9378.png)\n\nWhat is the range of the function $f(x)$, shown above?" 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186083526 1071 "![](images/e0/e07a67e287b43cad2785d717393a3868803b94dffed14040fdf1329dd6bc9378.p