ces $\\{A,B,C\\},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." 13194139535264 17592186045417 true] [17592186244002 1071 "Consider the set of matrices ${A,B,C},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." 13194139535264 17592186045417 false] [17592186244002 1074 "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{1} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} & -{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain